terms.medium_def:
A location first mentioned at Gen.12.10; 
referred to as Egypt or Egyptian (מִצְרַ֫יִם), or Egypt (מָצוֹר), or Egypt (KJV, NIV= "rebellion") (מְרִי), or Rahab (רַ֫הַב), or Egyptian or Egypt or Egyptian women or "they" (KJV= Egyptians) (מִצְרִי), or Ham (חָם), or Egypt (Αἴγυπτος), or Egyptian (Αἰγύπτιος). § a country at the northeastern section of Africa, adjacent to Palestine, and through which the Nile flows
Egyptians = "double straits"

A location first mentioned at Gen.12.10; 
referred to as Egypt or Egyptian (מִצְרַ֫יִם), or Egypt (מָצוֹר), or Egypt (KJV, NIV= "rebellion") (מְרִי), or Rahab (רַ֫הַב), or Egyptian or Egypt or Egyptian women or "they" (KJV= Egyptians) (מִצְרִי), or Ham (חָם), or Egypt (Αἴγυπτος), or Egyptian (Αἰγύπτιος). §"Matsor", a name for Egypt 
This name means siege, entrenchment

A man living at the time of the Patriarchs, first mentioned at Gen.10.6; 
only referred to as Egypt (מִצְרַ֫יִם); 
son of Ham; 
a brother of Canaan, Cush and Put; 
father of Ludim, Anamim, Lehabim, Naphtuhim, Pathrusim, Casluhim and Caphtorim.

A Governor living at the time of Divided Monarchy, first mentioned at 2Ki.25.22; 
referred to as Gedaliah (גְּדַלְיָ֫הוּ), or Gedaliah (גְּדַלְיָה); 
a son of Ahikam.

A location first mentioned at Num.34.6; 
referred to as Great_Sea or Great (Sea) (=Qere. Ketiv= "border," KJV= "the great sea," NIV= Mediterranean Sea) (גָּדוֹל), or (Sea of the )Philistines (NIV= Mediterranean Sea) (פְּלִשְׁתִּי). §adj
great

A Governor living at the time of Divided Monarchy, first mentioned at 2Ki.25.22; 
referred to as Gedaliah (גְּדַלְיָ֫הוּ), or Gedaliah (גְּדַלְיָה); 
a son of Ahikam.

A man from the tribe of Levi living at the time of United Monarchy, first mentioned at 1Ch.25.3; 
only referred to as Gedaliah (גְּדַלְיָ֫הוּ); 
son of Jeduthun; 
a brother of Obed-edom, Mattithiah, Zeri, Jeshaiah, Hashabiah.

A man from the tribe of Levi living at the time of Divided Monarchy, first mentioned at 1Ch.25.4; 
only referred to as Giddalti (גִּדַּלְתִּי); 
son of Heman; 
a brother of Bukkiah, Mattaniah, Uzziel, Shebuel, Jerimoth, Hananiah, Hanani, Eliathah, Romamti-ezer, Joshbekashah, Mallothi, Hothir, Mahazioth. § one of the sons of Heman, the king's seer

A priest living at the time of Exile and Return, only mentioned at Neh.11.14; 
only referred to as Haggedolim (גָּדוֹל);
father of Zabdiel. § (CLBL) Haggedolim, the great man?, father of Zabdiel

A man living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at Zep.1.1; 
only referred to as Gedaliah (גְּדַלְיָה); 
a son of Amariah; 
father of Cushi.

A man living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at Jer.38.1; 
only referred to as Gedaliah (גְּדַלְיָ֫הוּ); 
a son of Pashhur.

A man living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at Jer.35.4; 
only referred to as Igdaliah (יִגְדַּלְיָ֫הוּ); 
father of Hanan. § a prophet or holy man and father of Hanan in the time of Josiah

A location in Jerusalem first mentioned at Neh.3.1; 
only referred to as Tower_of_the_Hundred (מִגְדָּל מֵאָה). §
This name means tower

A man living at the time of United Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ki.4.19; 
only referred to as Geber (גֶּ֫בֶר); 
a son of Uri; 
father of Ben-Geber. § the son of Uri, an officer of Solomon, overseer of Gilead

A man living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, first mentioned at Num.1.6; 
only referred to as Zurishaddai (צוּרִישַׁדָּ֑י); 
father of Shelumiel. § father of Shelumiel, the chief of the Simeonites at the time of the exodus

A man from the tribe of Benjamin living at the time of United Monarchy, first mentioned at 1Ch.8.30; 
only referred to as Zur (צוּר); 
son of Abiel and Maacah; 
a brother of Kish, Ner, Abdon, Baal, Nadab, Gedor, Ahio, Zecher and Mikloth.

A man living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, only mentioned at Num.25.15; 
only referred to as Zur (צוּר); 
father of Cozbi.

A man living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, only mentioned at Num.3.35; 
only referred to as Zuriel (צוּרִיאֵל); 
a son of Abihail. § son of Abihail and chief of the Merarite Levites at the time of the exodus

A man of the Arabs living at the time of the Patriarchs, first mentioned at Gen.25.15; 
only referred to as Naphish (נָפִישׁ); 
son of Ishmael; 
a brother of Nebaioth, Kedar, Adbeel, Mibsam, Mishma, Dumah, Massa, Hadad, Tema, Jetur, Kedemah and Mahalath.

People from Naphtuh(?) of the Egyptians, first mentioned at Gen.10.13; 
only referred to as Naphtuhim (נַפְתֻּחִים); 
descended from Egypt along with Ludim, Anamim, Lehabim, Pathrusim, Casluhim and Caphtorim. § an unclear reference to Egypt; perhaps Lower Egypt

A man from the tribe of Levi living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, first mentioned at 1Ch.23.19; 
only referred to as Jekameam (יְקַמְעָם); 
son of Hebron; 
a brother of Jeriah, Amariah and Jahaziel. § a Levite, the 4th son of Hebron and grandson of Kohath in the time of David

A man from the tribe of Benjamin living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.8.19; 
only referred to as Jakim (יָקִים); 
son of Shimei; 
a brother of Zichri, Zabdi, Elienai, Zillethai, Eliel, Adaiah, Beraiah and Shimrath.

A man from the tribe of Judah living at the time of Divided Monarchy, first mentioned at 1Ch.2.41; 
only referred to as Jekamiah (יְקַמְיָה); 
a son of Shallum; 
father of Elishama.

A man from the tribe of Judah living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.3.18; 
only referred to as Jekamiah (יְקַמְיָה); 
son of Shealtiel(?); 
a brother of Malchiram, Pedaiah, Shenazzar, Hoshama and Nedabiah.

A king of Judah living at the time of Divided Monarchy, first mentioned at 2Ki.12.21; 
referred to as Amaziah or "he" (KJV= Amaziah) (אֲמַצְיָ֫הוּ); 
a son of Joash and Jehoaddan; 
husband of Jecoliah; 
father of Uzziah.

Isaiah's father living at the time of Divided Monarchy, first mentioned at 2Ki.19.2; 
only referred to as Amoz (אָמוֹץ); 
father of Isaiah. § father of Isaiah

A man from the tribe of Levi living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.6.46; 
only referred to as Amzi (אַמְצִי); 
a son of Bani; 
father of Hilkiah.

A priest living at the time of Exile and Return, only mentioned at Neh.11.12; 
only referred to as Amzi (אַמְצִי); 
a son of Zechariah; 
father of Pelaliah.

A man from the tribe of Simeon(?) living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.4.34; 
only referred to as Amaziah (אֲמַצְיָ֫הוּ); 
father of Joshah.

A man from the tribe of Levi living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.6.45; 
only referred to as Amaziah (אֲמַצְיָ֫הוּ); 
a son of Hilkiah; 
father of Hashabiah.

A man living at the time of the Patriarchs, first mentioned at Job.1.1; 
referred to as Job (אִיּוֹב), or Job (Ἰώβ); 
father of Jemimah, Keziah, Keren-happuch. § a patriarch, the subject of the book of Job

A man from the tribe of Judah living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, first mentioned at Gen.38.4; 
only referred to as Onan (אוֹנָן); 
son of Judah and Bath-shua ; 
a brother of Er and Shelah; 
half-brother of: Perez and Zerah. § second son of Judah, slain by God for not fulfilling the levitical requirement to beget a child with the wife of a dead, childless brother

A location first mentioned at 1Ch.8.12; 
referred to as Ono (אוֹנוֹ), or Hakkephirim (KJV, NIV= "villages") (כְּפִירִים). § city in Benjamin
♣2) a valley (of craftsman)

A man living at the time of the Patriarchs, first mentioned at Gen.36.23; 
only referred to as Onam (אוֹנָם); 
son of Shobal; 
a brother of Alvan, Manahath, Ebal and Shepho.

A man from the tribe of Judah living at the time of United Monarchy, first mentioned at 1Ch.2.26; 
only referred to as Onam (אוֹנָם); 
son of Jerahmeel and Atarah; 
a brother of Ram, Bunah, Oren, Ozem and Ahijah; 
father of Shammai and Jada.

A man living at the time of the Patriarchs, first mentioned at Gen.10.29; 
only referred to as Ophir (אוֹפִיר); 
son of Joktan; 
a brother of Almodad, Sheleph, Hazarmaveth, Jerah, Hadoram, Uzal, Diklah, Obal, Abimael, Sheba, Havilah and Jobab.

A man living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, only mentioned at Num.16.1; 
only referred to as On (אוֹן); 
a son of Peleth. § a chief of the tribe of Reuben

A location first mentioned at Deu.2.8; 
referred to as Elath (אֵילַת, אֵילוֹת), or Eloth (NIV= Elath) (אֵילוֹת). § grove of lofty trees 
a port on the north-east arm of the Red Sea

A king living at the time of Divided Monarchy, first mentioned at 1Ki.16.6; 
only referred to as Elah (אֵלָה); 
a son of Baasha. § a king of Israel for two years, son of Baasha

A man living at the time of Divided Monarchy, first mentioned at 2Ki.15.30; 
only referred to as Elah (אֵלָה); 
father of Hoshea. § the father of king Hoshea of Israel

A man from the tribe of Manasseh living at the time of Divided Monarchy, first mentioned at 1Ch.7.16; 
only referred to as Ulam (אוּלָם); 
son of Sheresh; 
a brother of Rakem; 
father of Bedan.

A man from the tribe of Benjamin living at the time of Divided Monarchy, first mentioned at 1Ch.8.39; 
only referred to as Ulam (אוּלָם); 
son of Eleasah; 
a brother of Jeush and Eliphelet.

A man living at the time of the Patriarchs, first mentioned at Gen.26.34; 
only referred to as Elon (אֵלוֹן); 
father of Adah.

A man from the tribe of Zebulun living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, first mentioned at Gen.46.14; 
referred to as Elon (אֵלוֹן), or Elonite (אֵלֹנִי); 
son of Zebulun; 
a brother of Sered and Jahleel.

A man from the tribe of Judah living before Israel's Monarchy, first mentioned at 1Ch.4.15; 
only referred to as Elah (אֵלָה); 
son of Caleb; 
a brother of Achsah, Iru and Naam; 
father of Kenaz and Jehallelel(?). §

A man living at the time of Exile and Return, only mentioned at 1Ch.9.8; 
only referred to as Elah (אֵלָה); 
a son of Uzzi. §

A man from the tribe of Zebulun living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, first mentioned at Gen.46.14; 
referred to as Elon (אֵלוֹן), or Elonite (אֵלֹנִי); 
son of Zebulun; 
a brother of Sered and Jahleel. § one of the clan of Elon

A king of Judah living at the time of Divided Monarchy, first mentioned at 2Ki.16.20; 
referred to as Hezekiah (חִזְקִיָּהוּ), or Hezekiah (KJV= Ezekias) (יְחִזְקִיָּה), or Hezekiah (Ἐζεκίας); 
son of Ahaz and Abi; 
a brother of Maaseiah; 
husband of Hephzibah; 
father of Manasseh.

A prophet living at the time of Exile and Return, first mentioned at Ezk.1.3; 
only referred to as Ezekiel (יְחֶזְקֵאל); 
a son of Buzi.

A king of Judah living at the time of Divided Monarchy, first mentioned at 2Ki.16.20; 
referred to as Hezekiah (חִזְקִיָּהוּ), or Hezekiah (KJV= Ezekias) (יְחִזְקִיָּה), or Hezekiah (Ἐζεκίας); 
son of Ahaz and Abi; 
a brother of Maaseiah; 
husband of Hephzibah; 
father of Manasseh.

A man from the tribe of Benjamin living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.8.17; 
only referred to as Hizki (חִזְקִי); 
son of Elpaal; 
a brother of Eber, Misham, Shemed, Beriah, Shema, Zebadiah, Meshullam, Heber, Ishmerai, Izliah and Jobab. § a Benjamite, descendant of Shaaraim

A man from the tribe of Judah living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.3.23; 
only referred to as Hizkiah (חִזְקִיָּהוּ); 
son of Neariah; 
a brother of Elioenai and Azrikam.

A man living at the time of Exile and Return, first mentioned at Ezr.2.16; 
referred to as Hezekiah (חִזְקִיָּהוּ), or Hezekiah (יְחִזְקִיָּה); 
a son of Ater.

A man living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at Zep.1.1; 
only referred to as Hezekiah (חִזְקִיָּהוּ); 
father of Amariah.

A man living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 2Ch.28.12; 
only referred to as Jehizkiah (יְחִזְקִיָּה); 
a son of Shallum.

A man living at the time of Exile and Return, first mentioned at Ezr.2.16; 
referred to as Hezekiah (חִזְקִיָּהוּ), or Hezekiah (יְחִזְקִיָּה); 
a son of Ater.

A king of Judah living at the time of Divided Monarchy, first mentioned at 2Ki.14.21; 
referred to as Uzziah (עֻזִּיָּהוּ), or Azariah (עֲזַרְיָה), or Azariah (עֲזַרְיָ֫הוּ), or Uzziah (KJV= Ozias) (Ὀζίας); 
a son of Amaziah and Jecoliah; 
husband of Jerusha; 
father of Jotham.

Aaron's uncle from the tribe of Levi living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, first mentioned at Exo.6.18; 
referred to as Uzziel (עֻזִּיאֵל), or Uzzielite (עׇזִּיאֵלִי); 
son of Kohath; 
a brother of Amram, Izhar and Hebron; 
father of Mishael, Elizaphan, Sithri, Micah and Isshiah.

A man living at the time of United Monarchy, first mentioned at 2Sa.6.3; 
referred to as Uzzah or Uzzah (עֻזָּא), or Perez-uzzah (NIV= Perez Uzzah) (פֶּרֶץ עֻזָּא); 
son of Abinadab; 
a brother of Eleazar and Ahio.

A High Priest from the tribe of Levi living at the time of Divided Monarchy, first mentioned at 1Ch.6.5; 
only referred to as Uzzi (עֻזִּי); 
a son of Bukki; 
father of Zerahiah.

A man from the tribe of Levi living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, first mentioned at 1Ch.24.26; 
only referred to as Jaaziah (יַעֲזִיָּ֫הוּ); 
son of Merari; 
a brother of Mahli and Mushi; 
father of Beno, Shoham, Zaccur and Ibri. § a Levite, apparently the 3rd son or a descendant of Merari

A man from the tribe of Issachar living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, first mentioned at 1Ch.7.2; 
only referred to as Uzzi (עֻזִּי); 
son of Tola; 
a brother of Rephaiah, Jeriel, Jahmai, Ibsam and Shemuel; 
father of Izrahiah.

Aaron's uncle from the tribe of Levi living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, first mentioned at Exo.6.18; 
referred to as Uzziel (עֻזִּיאֵל), or Uzzielite (עׇזִּיאֵלִי); 
son of Kohath; 
a brother of Amram, Izhar and Hebron; 
father of Mishael, Elizaphan, Sithri, Micah and Isshiah. § Uzzielites, of Uzziel "my strength is God"
descendants of Uzziel

A man from the tribe of Benjamin living at the time of Divided Monarchy, first mentioned at 1Ch.8.36; 
only referred to as Azmaveth (עַזְמָ֫וֶת); 
son of Jehoaddah; 
a brother of Alemeth and Zimri.

A man from the tribe of Levi living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.6.29; 
only referred to as Uzzah (עֻזָּה); 
a son of Shimei; 
father of Shimea. § a Merarite Levite

A man from the tribe of Benjamin living before Israel's Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.8.7; 
only referred to as Uzza (עֻזָּא); 
son of Ehud; 
a brother of Naaman, Ahijah, Gera and Ahihud. § a Merarite Levite

A man living at the time of Exile and Return, only mentioned at Neh.3.16; 
only referred to as Azbuk (עַזְבּוּק); 
father of Nehemiah. § father of Nehemiah, leader of half the district of Beth Zur, and a repairer of the walls of Jerusalem under another Nehemiah

A man from the tribe of Reuben living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.5.8; 
only referred to as Azaz (עָזָז); 
a son of Shema; 
father of Bela. § a Reubenite, father of Bela

A man living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.27.20; 
only referred to as Azaziah (עֲזַזְיָ֫הוּ); 
father of Hoshea.

A man from the tribe of Benjamin living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, only mentioned at 1Ch.7.7; 
only referred to as Uzzi (עֻזִּי); 
son of Bela; 
a brother of Ard, Naaman, Ezbon, Uzziel, Jerimoth, Iri, Addar, Gera, Abihud, Abishua and Ahoah.

A man living at the time of Exile and Return, only mentioned at 1Ch.9.8; 
only referred to as Uzzi (עֻזִּי); 
a son of Michri; 
father of Elah.

A man living at the time of Exile and Return, only mentioned at Neh.11.22; 
only referred to as Uzzi (עֻזִּי); 
a son of Bani.

A man from the tribe of Simeon(?) living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.4.42; 
only referred to as Uzziel (עֻזִּיאֵל); 
son of Ishi; 
a brother of Pelatiah, Neariah and Rephaiah.

A man from the tribe of Benjamin living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, only mentioned at 1Ch.7.7; 
only referred to as Uzziel (עֻזִּיאֵל); 
son of Bela; 
a brother of Ard, Naaman, Ezbon, Uzzi, Jerimoth, Iri, Addar, Gera, Abihud, Abishua and Ahoah.

A man from the tribe of Levi living at the time of Divided Monarchy, first mentioned at 1Ch.25.4; 
referred to as Uzziel (עֻזִּיאֵל), or Azarel (KJV= Azareel) (עֲזַרְאֵל); 
son of Heman; 
a brother of Bukkiah, Mattaniah, Shebuel, Jerimoth, Hananiah, Hanani, Eliathah, Giddalti, Romamti-ezer, Joshbekashah, Mallothi, Hothir and Mahazioth.

A man from the tribe of Levi living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 2Ch.29.14; 
only referred to as Uzziel (עֻזִּיאֵל); 
son of Jeduthun; 
a brother of Shemaiah.

A man living at the time of Exile and Return, only mentioned at Neh.3.8; 
only referred to as Uzziel (עֻזִּיאֵל); 
a son of Harhaiah.

A man from the tribe of Levi living at the time of Divided Monarchy, first mentioned at 1Ch.6.24; 
referred to as Uzziah (עֻזִּיָּהוּ), or Azariah (עֲזַרְיָ֫הוּ); 
a son of Uriel; 
father of Shaul.

A man living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.27.25; 
only referred to as Uzziah (עֻזִּיָּהוּ); 
father of Jonathan.

A man living at the time of Exile and Return, only mentioned at Neh.11.4; 
only referred to as Uzziah (עֻזִּיָּהוּ); 
a son of Zechariah; 
father of Athaiah.

A man living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.12.3; 
only referred to as Azmaveth (עַזְמָ֫וֶת); 
father of Jeziel, Pelet.

A man living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.27.25; 
only referred to as Azmaveth (עַזְמָ֫וֶת); 
a son of Adiel.

A man living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, only mentioned at Num.34.26; 
only referred to as Azzan (עַזָּן); 
father of Paltiel. § father of Paltiel prince of the tribe of Issachar who represented his tribe in the division of the promised land

A Singer from the tribe of Levi living at the time of United Monarchy, first mentioned at 1Ch.6.44; 
referred to as Jeduthun or Jeduthun (=Qere. Ketiv= Jedithun) (יְדוּתוּן), or Ethan (אֵיתָן); 
a son of Kishi; 
father of Obed-edom, Mattithiah, Gedaliah, Zeri, Jeshaiah, Hashabiah, Shemaiah and Uzziel.

A man living at the time of United Monarchy, first mentioned at 1Ki.4.31; 
only referred to as Ethan (אֵיתָן); 
son of Mahol; 
a brother of Heman, Calcol and Darda.

A man from the tribe of Judah living before Israel's Monarchy, first mentioned at 1Ch.2.6; 
only referred to as Ethan (אֵיתָן); 
son of Zerah; 
a brother of Zabdi, Heman, Calcol and Dara; 
father of Azariah.

A man from the tribe of Levi living at the time of Divided Monarchy, first mentioned at 1Ch.6.21; 
referred to as Joah (יוֹאָח), or Ethan (אֵיתָן); 
a son of Zimmah; 
father of Iddo.

A man from the tribe of Judah living at the time of Divided Monarchy, first mentioned at 1Ch.2.39; 
only referred to as Helez (חֶ֫לֶץ); 
a son of Azariah; 
father of Eleasah.
